<%- include('_head', { title: 'Help guide' }) %>
<div class="topbar"><div><h1>Help guide</h1><p>Quick answers for the most common jobs.</p></div></div>
<div class="two"><div>
<div class="card"><h2>A room has been taken</h2><p>Go to <a href="/admin/c/rooms">Rooms</a> and change its status to <b>Let / allocated</b>. It disappears from the website straight away. Change it back to <b>Available now</b> when it's free again, and all its photos and details are kept.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Add a new room</h2><p><a href="/admin/c/rooms/new">Add room</a> → fill in the details → drag in photos → Save. A reference like <b>SH-107</b> is created automatically and included in every WhatsApp enquiry.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Advertise a room on Facebook</h2><p>Open the room in admin and copy the <b>Facebook advert link</b>. Put that link in your post or advert. People land on the room page with a green WhatsApp button, and the enquiry arrives on WhatsApp with the room reference already in the message.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Change words or photos on a page</h2><p>Open the website while logged in and press <b>Edit this page</b> at the bottom. Click any heading or paragraph and type. Changes save when you click away. Click a photo to replace it or choose which part stays in view. You can also use <a href="/admin/content">Page text & images</a>.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Photos look badly cropped</h2><p>Click on the photo in its edit screen to move the pink dot onto the important part, such as someone's face or the bed. The website keeps that spot visible on every screen size.</p></div>
</div><div>
<div class="card"><h2>Events & bookings</h2><p>Add an event with a number of spaces. The website counts down the spaces and shows <b>Fully booked</b> automatically. See who's coming, add phone bookings and download the list from <b>View registrations</b>.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Replace the referral form</h2><p>Go to <a href="/admin/c/documents">Documents</a> → Referral form → <b>Replace file</b> → Save. The download link on the website stays the same.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Tenants' stories & consent</h2><p>A story only appears once the consent box is ticked. Use first names or initials, and remove a story straight away if someone asks by switching off <b>Show on website</b>.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Repair reports & messages</h2><p>They all arrive in the <a href="/admin/inbox">Inbox</a> and by email once it's set up in <a href="/admin/settings">Settings</a>. Mark them as <b>Resolved</b> when they're done and add internal notes for the team.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Formatting longer text</h2><p>Leave a blank line between paragraphs. Start a line with <code>- </code> for bullet points. Put text between <code>**double stars**</code> for bold. Links use <code>[link text](https://address)</code>.</p></div>
</div></div>
